Subject: [PATCH 2/2] B1: multi-shift GDT counting theorem, kernel-checked

Adds the Challenge/Solution pair MultiShift with seven statements: the
dichotomy, the period Tmin = mR, the exact count prod_{p | R}(p - nu_p(H))
per period, the density decomposition, the absolute density
(1/m) prod (1 - nu_p(H)/p), the H = {0} specialization, and GDT v1.0.0's
gdt_count_per_period re-derived through the multi-shift theorem. A
build-time check confirms that statement is GDT's exactly (Gate B).

Track B requires Mathlib at 85e3a25, the commit GDT v1.0.0 pins. GDT's
definitions and lemmas are vendored with provenance hashes, because a
package dependency collides with GDT's Challenge/Solution libraries.
Track A pairs import neither and keep their trusted base.

